1032,501434,Hellespont (strait),"The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Dardanelles/Çanakkale Boğazı TKY The Hellespont is a narrow strait of northwestern Turkey that connects the Aegean Sea to the Propontis (Sea of Marmara). It is known today as the Dardanelles. Pseudo-Apollodorus records a myth that seems to have been widespread in antiquity: the Hellespont got its name by being the place where Helle, sister of Phrixus, fell off the flying golden ram."
1033,501439,Imbros (island),The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Gökçeada TKY The island of Imbros (modern Gökçeada in Turkey) was colonized by Athens in antiquity.
