1060,507469,Stratoni (Stratonikeia/Stratonike?),"The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: E Khalkidike Recent archaeological survey and excavation have identified structures, artifacts, and Hellenistic pottery just west of the modern Greek village of Stratoni, on the north-eastern coast of the Chalkidiki peninsula. Excavators argue that these should be taken as reinforcing an association between the modern name Stratoni and the ancient Macedonian polis of Stratonike, which is attested in ancient sources."
1061,507470,Syleos Pedion,The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: near Stageira A plain near Stageira across which Xerxes passed en route to Acanthus.
1062,507480,Zereia/Zeira,The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Khalkidike Diodorus refers to Zereia/Zeira as a fortress and places it near the location of Chalcidice. It was razed by Philip V. It is now unlocated. (cited: BAtlas 51 unlocated Zereia/Zeira)
