1363,550756,Myrina/Sebastopolis,"The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: mouth of Koca Çay An ancient place, cited: BAtlas 56 D4 Myrina/Sebastopolis"
1364,550763,Mytilene,"The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Mytilene, on Lesbos GRE An ancient settlement. The early fortified core of the city was located on an islet off the east coast of Lesbos, now joined to the mainland. That site is dominated by the remains of a Byzantine fortress with Ottoman and Genoese repairs and additions. This original city later expanded onto the main island."
1365,550771,Naulochon/Smyrna/Palaia Smyrna,"The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Bayraklı An ancient settlement located on the gulf of Smyrna, east of the town of Bayraklı (some 4 km north of Izmir, Turkey). Archaeological evidence indicates that the earliest Hellenic evidence dates to the eleventh or tenth centuries B.C."
1366,550773,Neonteichos,"The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Yanıkköy? An ancient place, cited: BAtlas 56 E4 Neonteichos"
1367,550787,Ophryneion,"The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: near Erenköy The legendary founder of the site is Akamas. Ophryneion was an ancient city of the northern Troad. It lay between Rhoteum and Dardanus. The site is located about 1.5 km north-east of the village of İntepe (previously known as Erenköy) in Çanakkale Province, Turkey."
1368,550793,Allianoi,"According to press reports, this site was briefly excavated prior to being flooded behind the Bergama Yortanlı dam in 2011. An ancient spa, known in modern times as Paşa Ilıca in Turkey."
1369,550794,Pactolus (river),"The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Sart Çay An ancient place, cited: BAtlas 56 G5 Pactolus fl."
1370,550804,Parthenion,"The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Eski Bergama A settlement attested in ancient sources, that was probably located along the modern Ilias Çay in Turkey, downstream from the modern Yortanlı dam."
1371,550808,Pelekas M.,"The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: between Balıkesir and Simav Çay An ancient place, cited: BAtlas 56 G2 Pelekas M."
1372,550812,Pergamum,"The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Bergama An important ancient settlement, located at modern Bergama in Turkey. It was first described in Xenophon's Anabasis and was later used as a treasury under Lysimachus. Pergamum became the administrative capital and principal city of the Attalid kingdom and dynasty (282-133 BCE) and was briefly the first capital of the Roman province of Asia. It later was a seat of a Christian bishopric and is listed in Revelation as one of the seven churches of Asia. It was inscribed as a UNESCO World Heritage Site in 2014 under ""Pergamon and its Multi-Layered Cultural Landscape""."
1373,550822,Philadelpheia,"The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Alaşehir An ancient settlement of Asia Minor, modern Alaşehir, Turkey."
1374,550830,Pindasos (mountain),The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Madra Dağ An ancient mountain in Mysia: the modern Madra Daği in Turkey.
1375,550832,Pionia(i),"The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Gömeniç An ancient place, cited: BAtlas 56 F2 Pionia(i)"
