1383,550867,Sardis/Hyde?,"The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Sart Sardis was the capital of the Lydian Empire, located in western Turkey. In 188 B.C. Sardis became a part of the Attalid kingdom, and thus it passed with the territory of Attalus III to Rome in 133 B.C."
