1482,570264,Glaukos (river),"The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Leuka/Glaukos An ancient place, cited: BAtlas 58 B1 Glaukos fl."
1483,570265,Glyppia,"The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Ag. Vasileios An ancient place, cited: BAtlas 58 D3 Glyppia"
1484,570266,Gortynios/Lousios (river),The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Lousios A river of the Peloponnese.
1485,570267,Gortys,"The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: between Atsicholo and Helleniko An ancient place, cited: BAtlas 58 C2 Gortys"
1486,570274,Halieis,"A web page with history and reminiscences of the American excavations at Halieis (1962-1980), including many photographs and a scholarly bibliography, is available: Halieis (specifically, House 7) is planned as an interactive web environment at Archaeology magazine's Dig Greece website, see: . An ancient Greek harbor city in the Argolid (across from the modern village of Porto Cheli) that was abandoned toward the end of the fourth century BCE. Excavated remains include fortification walls (as early as the eighth century BCE), a city with an orthogonal street plan, an industrial quarter, and domestic architecture with evidence for agricultural processing. Parts of the city are now under water due to a rise in sea levels."
1487,570278,Harpina,"The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: near Miraka Harpina, an ancient city of Elis, just east of Olympia, is mentioned in ancient sources. It is thought to have been located at a site just north of modern Archaia Pisa (Miraka)."
1488,570281,Helike,"The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: E Aigion An ancient place, cited: BAtlas 58 C1 Helike"
1489,570282,Helisson,"The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: near Alonistaina An ancient polis mentioned by Pausanias. Epigraphic evidence indicates that, in the 5th century BCE, it became a political dependency of Mantinea. Its precise location is not known, but Camp in BAtlDir followed some earlier scholarship in placing it ""near Alonistaina,"" a modern village in the municipality of Falanthos (Arcadia)."
1490,570283,Helisson (river in modern Sikyona municipality),"The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Lechora An ancient river of the Peloponnese, mentioned by Pausanias. It empties into the Corinthian Gulf and is identified with the modern Elissonas in the Greek municipality of Sikyona."
1491,570284,Helisson (river in modern Megalopoli),"The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Helisson An ancient river of the Peloponnese, mentioned by Pausanias, who describes it as contributary of the Aminius and a tributary of the Alpheius. The modern Elissonas river in the Greek municipality of Megalopoli is identified with this ancient river."
1492,570286,Helos?,"The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Ag. Stephanos An ancient place, cited: BAtlas 58 D4 Helos?"
1493,570287,Heraia,"The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Ag. Ioannes An ancient city of Arcadia, located on the north bank of the Alpheius river, east of its confluence with the Ladon. Archaeological evidence for its location has been identified near modern Hagios Ioannis."
1494,570289,Heraion (Argolis),The Argive Heraion was a major ancient sanctuary sacred to Hera located in the Argolid.
1495,570292,Hermion(e),The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Ermione Hermion(e) was a settlement of the eastern Argolid.
1496,570296,Hormina? M.,"The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Chlemoutsi/Kounoupelli An ancient place, cited: BAtlas 58 A2 Hormina? M."
1497,570302,Hyperteleaton,"The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Chasanaga Sanctuary of Apollo Hyperteleatas, partially excavated in 1885 and 1968. In ancient literature the sanctuary is only mentioned by Pausanias, in whose time it was called the Hyperteleaton and was dedicated to Asclepius. The site is located south of Phoiniki in the southeastern Peloponnese at a place known in the 19th century called Chasanaga."
1498,570304,Hypsous (mountain),The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Klinitsa/Hypsous Klinitsa/Hypsous.
1499,570306,Hysiai,"The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Akhladokampos Hysiai was a frontier citadel of Argos located to the south of the modern village of Achladokampos. The Lacedaemonians destroyed the site in 417 B.C. Pausanias visited the ruined settlement, while Curtius described the remains of the fortifications."
1500,570315,Ipnoi (mountain),"The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Kaminia, on Keos A mountain, probably Kaminia, on Keos."
1501,570321,Kaiadas Spelaion,"The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: prison cave at Trypi The Kaiadas cave is located near modern Trypi in the Peloponnese. Ancient testimony identifies it as a place of execution used by the ancient Spartans. Exploration in the modern era identified a significant number of skeletal remains, but these have not been effectively dated."
1502,570323,Kalamai,"The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Perivolakia/Sola An ancient place, cited: BAtlas 58 C3 Kalamai"
1503,570325,Kalaureia (island),"The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Poros An island near the coast of Troezen in the Peloponnesus, now known as Poros."
1504,570330,Kardamyle (Messenia),"The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Kardamyle An ancient place, cited: BAtlas 58 C4 Kardamyle"
1505,570332,Karnion (river),"The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Xerilas An ancient place, cited: BAtlas 58 C3 Karnion fl."
1506,570336,Karystos,"The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: settlement and marble quarries in Euboea Karystos was a Greek polis located on the south coast of Euboea. It is included in Homer's ""catalogue of ships"" in the Iliad, and its name is also thought to be attested in Linear B documents. The ancient acropolis hill, which lies to the north of the modern coastal village, is now occupied by the remains of the Venetian ""Castel Rosso""."
1507,570345,Kelossa (mountain),The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Megalovouni The mountain known in antiquity as Kelossa is the modern Megalovouni to the southwest of Nemea.
1508,570347,Kenchreai,"The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Kechriai, in Corinthia The ancient Saronic Gulf port of Corinth (near modern Kechries in Greece)."
1509,570354,Keryneia,The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Mamousia An ancient city located on a hill immediately north of the modern Greek village of Mamousia (Achaea).
1510,570355,Kerynitis (river),"The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Bouraikos An ancient place, cited: BAtlas 58 C1 Kerynitis fl."
1511,570358,Kladeos (river),"The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Kladeos A river of the Peloponnese and tributary of the Alpheios, which it joins from the north at the ancient site of Olympia in Greece."
1512,570360,Kleitor (river),"The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Mostitsaiiko An ancient place, cited: BAtlas 58 C2 Kleitor fl."
1513,570361,Kleonai,"The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Ag. Vasileios/Kleonai An ancient city located in the mountainous area southwest of Corinth. The acropolis of ancient Kleonai lies about two kilometers east of the modern town named after it in the 1960s (Archaies Kleones, formerly Kontostavlos)."
1514,570363,Knakalos (mountain),"The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Kastania An ancient place, cited: BAtlas 58 C2 Knakalos M."
1515,570369,Kolyergia (promuntory),"The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Cape Miliaros An ancient place, cited: BAtlas 58 E3 Kolyergia Pr."
1516,570371,Korone,The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Petalidhi Korone was located on the west coast of the Messenian Gulf at the foot of Mount Mathia. Modern Petalidi.
1517,570375,Koryphasion (promuntory),"The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Akr. Koryphasiou An ancient place, cited: BAtlas 58 B4 Koryphasion Pr."
1518,570379,Kranae (island),"The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Marathonisi, near Gythion Kranae is an island off the coast of Gytheio."
1519,570380,Kraneion,The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: grove near Corinth Pausanias describes the Kraneion as a grove of cypress trees located on the outskirts of Corinth.
1520,570381,Krathis (river),"The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Krathis The Krathis is a river of Achaea. Achaean Aegae lies close to the river course, which is discussed by Herodotus, Strabo, and Pausanias."
1521,570385,Krokeai,The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Krokees Krokeai was a settlement in southern Laconia.
1522,570387,Kromna,"The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: W Ag. Demetrios An ancient settlement located between Kenchreai and Korinth. Archaeological survey and excavation reveal a rich record of human occupation from the Neolithic period onward in the area around modern Hexamilia. The Archaic through Hellenistic center seems to have been concentrated east of Hexamilia in the area of modern Kesimia (just west of Ag. Demetrios), with a possible subsequent Roman-era shift to the southwest around Monastiraki."
1523,570390,Kyllene,"The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Kyllini An ancient place, cited: BAtlas 58 A2 Kyllene"
1524,570391,Kyllene (mountain),"The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Mt. Kyllene A mountain in Arcadia (Greece), still known as Kyllene today."
1525,570396,Kyparissia,"The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Boza An ancient settlement of Laconia in the Peloponnese, identified by modern scholars with the modern Boza plateau and the west-facing bay below it (northwest of ancient Asopos). The area has produced archaeological evidence dating from the bronze age to late Roman."
1526,570397,Kyparissia,The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Kyparissia Kyparissia was an ancient settlement of Messenia.
1527,570399,Kyther(i)os (river),"The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Pournaraiiko An ancient place, cited: BAtlas 58 B2 Kyther(i)os fl."
1528,570403,Kythnos (island),The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Kythnos Herodotus states that the island was originally colonized by the Dryopes. Kythnos is an island in the Aegean Sea and one of the Cyclades.
1529,570406,Lacedaemon/Laconia,The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Lakonia Lacedaemon/Laconia is a region comprising the south-eastern part of the Peloponnese.
1530,570410,Lampeia (mountain),The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Mt. Kalliphoniou Mt. Kalliphoniou.
1531,570413,Lapithaion,"The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Anogeia? An ancient place, cited: BAtlas 58 C4 Lapithaion"
1532,570414,Lapithos (mountain),The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Lapithas Mount Lapithas.
1533,570415,Larisos (river),The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Larisas/Manna An ancient river of the northern Peloponnese that was considered to constitute the western border of the region of Achaia.
1534,570416,Larysion (mountain),The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Mt. Koumarou Mt. Koumarou.
1535,570417,La(s),"The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Passavas An ancient place, cited: BAtlas 58 D4 La(s)"
1536,570421,Leon,The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Vigla Modern Cape Vigla on Euboea.
1537,570423,Lepreon,The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Lepreon An ancient city of Elis.
1538,570424,Lerna,The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: S Myloi Lerna was an ancient settlement on the east coast of the Peloponnesus. Extensive Bronze Age layers were excavated in the twentieth century by J. L. Caskey.
1539,570426,Lessa,"The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Kazarma At Lessa, Pausanias observed a sanctuary sacred to Athena where a wooden cult image was to be seen."
1540,570427,Letrinoi,"The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Pyrgos? An ancient place, cited: BAtlas 58 A2 Letrinoi"
1541,570429,Leuke,"An ancient place, cited: BAtlas 58 D4 Leuke"
1542,570431,Leuktron,The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Stoupa Leuktron was an ancient settlement in the southern Peloponnese. Pausanias places it twenty stades from Pephnus.
1543,570433,Leuktron,The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Leontari Leuktron in Arcadia.
1544,570434,Leukyanias (river),"The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: river An ancient place, cited: BAtlas 58 B2 Leukyanias fl."
1545,570438,Lousoi,"The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Lousiko/Chamakou A settlement in Azania, located near modern Kato Lusi, that has been under excavation since the late 19th century."
1546,570441,Lykaion (mountain),"The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Lykaion Mount Lykaion is located in Arcadia. As a sacred site, Lykaion is thought to be the birthplace of Zeus and the home of Pan. Parrhasian Apollo was worshipped on the eastern slopes."
1547,570442,Lykoa,"The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Zarachova/Mainalo? An ancient place, cited: BAtlas 58 C2 Lykoa"
1548,570443,Lykone (mountain),The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: spur of Megavouni A spur of Megavouni.
1549,570444,Lykosoura,The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Lykosoura. A city of Arcadia and home of the cult of Despoina
1550,570445,Lykouria?,"The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Lykouria According to Pausanias, Lykouria? is located in Arcadia and marks the boundary between Pheneus and Cleitor."
1551,570447,Lyrkeion (mountain),The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Lyrkeion Lyrkeion.
1552,570449,Mainalion (mountain),"The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Mainalon The tallest in Arcadia, Mainalion is part of the Menalon mountain range of the Peloponnese."
1553,570451,Mainalos,"The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: near Daria An ancient settlement of Arcadia, abandoned by Pausanias' day. Probably to be located near Daria."
1554,570454,Malea,"The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Boutsaras, formerly Zaime An ancient place, cited: BAtlas 58 C3 Malea"
1555,570455,Malea Pr.,The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Akr. Maleas Cape Maleas is a cape located in the southeast of the Peloponnese.
1556,570457,Maloitas (river),"The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: near Methydrion The Maloitas river, mentioned by Pausanias and placed by him near Methydrion in the Peloponnese, was identified by F. Bölte in RE with a small, intermittent tributary of the modern Trogas river that lies between Methydrion and modern Pyrgaki, which is located in the modern Greek municipal unit of Vytina (Arcadia regional unit). BAtlas cites Pausanias and labels linework corresponding to this stream."
1557,570459,Mantineia/Antigoneia,The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Mantineia Mantineia/Antigoneia was an ancient settlement in Greece most noted for being the site of two major battles. The First Battle of Mantineia was the largest land battle of the Peloponnesian War (418 B.C.) and the Second Battle of Mantineia brought an end to Theban hegemony (362 B.C.).
1558,570461,Marios,"The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Mari An ancient place, cited: BAtlas 58 D3 Marios"
1559,570464,Mathia (mountain),The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Lykodemos A mountain of the Peloponnese mentioned by Pausanias. Modern Lykodemos.
1560,570468,Megara,"The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Megara Megara was an important ancient city of Greece, located in the northern part of the the Isthmus of Corinth opposite the island of Salamis."
1561,570470,Megaris,"The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Megarid An ancient place, cited: BAtlas 58 E2 Megaris"
1562,570471,Meiganitas (river),"The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Gaidaropnichtes An ancient place, cited: BAtlas 58 C1 Meiganitas fl."
1563,570473,Melangeia,"The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Pikerni An ancient place, cited: BAtlas 58 C2 Melangeia"
1564,570475,Melos (island),The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Melos Is. Melos is a volcanic island in the Cyclades and in prehistoric times served as an important source of obsidian in the Aegean Sea. Substantial remains of Bronze Age and Greco-Roman civilizations have been excavated on the island.
1565,570476,Melpeia,"The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: on Mt. Lykaion An ancient place, cited: BAtlas 58 B3 Melpeia"
1566,570477,Menelaion,The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Aphisiou An ancient Greek sanctuary of Helen and Menelaos near ancient Therapnai in Greece.
1567,570478,Messa,"The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Cape Tigani An ancient place, cited: BAtlas 58 C4 Messa"
1568,570482,Methana/Arsinoe,"The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: below Megalochori Methana/Arsinoe refers to a peninsula and settlement located on the north coast of the Argolid. In geological terms, the peninsula is formed by relatively recent volcanic activity, with the last-known eruptive activity in the third century BCE. Human activity on the peninsula spans many periods. The chief polity was located in the southwest of the peninsula where the modern village of Megalochori is found today."
1569,570483,Methone/Mothone (Messenian),"The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Methoni An ancient settlement situated on the west coast of the Messenian peninsula of the Peloponnese. The collocated modern settlement is called Methoni and is located in the administrative part of the Pylos-Nestoras municipality, Messenia regional unit, of the modern Greek state."
1570,570486,Minoa (island),"The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Pachakion Modern Pachaki island, just off the Greek coast in the Saronic Gulf opposite the airport of the modern city of Megara."
1571,570487,Minoa (promontory),"The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Monemvasia The ""tied island"" known today as Monemvasia, located along the southeast coast of the Peloponnese. Pausanias referred to it as ""Akra Minoa""."
1572,570491,Mycenae,"The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Mykenes. Mycenae has been the site of extensive excavations during the nineteenth and twentieth centuries. Fieldwork there continues to the present day. Mycenae was an ancient settlement of the Argolid, with the earliest occupation evident ca. 2900 B.C. As the eponymous site of the Mycenaean culture of the Aegean Bronze Age, the site flourished as a fortified citadel during the mid to late second millennium B.C. In the first millennium B.C., the site experienced a revival of fortunes, although by Strabo's time the settlement had vanished."
1573,570494,Myrsinos/Myrtountion?,"The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: 70 stades from Elis An ancient place, cited: BAtlas 58 A1 Myrsinos/Myrtountion?"
1574,570495,Myrtoion Mare,The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Myrtoion pelagos Myrtoion Mare (Myrtoan Sea) is a part of the Mediterranean Sea lying between the Cyclades and the Peloponnese.
1575,570498,Mysia (settlement),"The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Phyktia? An ancient settlement in the Argolid, mentioned by Pausanias, who highlights there a sanctuary of Demeter. This settlement is probably to be identified with the modern Phyktia."
1576,570501,Nauplia,"The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Nauplion Although the Classical/Hellenistic city was deserted in Pausanias' day, archaeology reveals that the area of modern Nafplio and its natural harbor on the Argolic Gulf was repeatedly a site of habitation and human activity from the Neolithic period to the modern day. Remains of a Hellenistic acropolis wall have been identified under the later Byzantine (with subsequent accretions and modifications) fort."
1577,570502,Neda (river),"The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Bouzi A river of Greece, rising on the slopes of Mt. Lykaion and flowing west to empty into the Gulf of Kyparissia just south of the modern village of Giannitsochori."
1578,570504,Nemea,"The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Herakleion Nemea, located north of Argos, was the site of the Panhellenic Games and the Sanctuary of Nemean Zeus."
1579,570505,Nemea (river),"The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Zapantis/Nemea Today an intermittent drainage known as the Nemeas or Zapantis that rises in the vicinity of ancient Nemea and flows north, emptying into the Corinthian Gulf near the modern village of Vrachati."
1580,570506,Neris?,"The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Kato Doliana An ancient place, cited: BAtlas 58 D3 Neris?"
1581,570508,Nisaia,"The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: near Pachi An ancient place, cited: BAtlas 58 E2 Nisaia"
1582,570511,Nymphaion,"The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Ag. Marina? An ancient coastal settlement in Lakonia (Peloponnese), tentatively identified in BAtlas with the area of modern Ag. Marina."
1583,570523,Oinous (river),"The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Kelephina, near Sellasia An ancient river of the Peloponnese peninsula that flows into the Eurotas River near the site of Sparta."
1584,570524,Oinoussai (islands),"The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Sapientza, Schiza et al. An ancient place, cited: BAtlas 58 B4 Oinoussai Inss."
1585,570527,Oitylos,"The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Oitylos. Pausanias reports that a wooden image ( xoanon ) of Apollo Carneius was to be seen in the agora. An ancient place, cited: BAtlas 58 C4 Oitylos"
1586,570528,Olenos,"The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Tsoukalaiika/Kamenitsa? An ancient place, cited: BAtlas 58 B1 Olenos"
1587,570529,Olmiai Pr.,"The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Schinas An ancient place, cited: BAtlas 58 E1 Olmiai Pr."
1588,570531,Olympia,The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Archaia Olympia Ancient sanctuary of Zeus and home of the ancient Olympic games.
1589,570532,Oneon (mountain),"The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Stanotopi An ancient place, cited: BAtlas 58 D2 Oneon M."
1590,570533,Onougnathos (promontory),"The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Ag. Maria/Elaphonisas This ancient cape of the Peloponnese is now known as the island of Elaphonisas, separated from the mainland reportedly by a fourth-century earthquake. The island's southwestern terminus -- the modern Akra Ag. Maria -- would correspond to the tip of the ancient promontory."
1591,570534,Ophis (river),"The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Pheidias An ancient place, cited: BAtlas 58 C2 Ophis fl."
1592,570535,Orchomenos (Arcadia),"The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Kalpaki. Not to be confused with Boeotian Orchomenos . The so-called ""Arcadian Orchomenos"", located near a modern village in the Peloponnese that, until the 1960s, was known as Kalpaki."
1593,570537,Orneai,"The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: above Lyrkeia An ancient place, cited: BAtlas 58 D2 Orneai"
1594,570543,Pagai,The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Alepochori A fortified port located on the Gulf of Corinth near Alepokhori.
1595,570545,Palaia/Pleiai,"The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: SW Apidea An ancient place, cited: BAtlas 58 D4 Palaia/Pleiai"
1596,570548,Pallantion,"The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Berbati An ancient settlement located just west of the modern Greek city that has borne the ancient name since the 20th century (previously Berbati). Archaeological evidence confirms continuous habitation from the archaic through the Byzantine periods, and there is plentiful evidence in the surrounding area for activity beginning in the Mycenaean period."
1597,570550,Pamisos (river),"The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Milia An ancient place, cited: BAtlas 58 C4 Pamisos fl."
1598,570551,Pamisos (river of Messenia),The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Pamisos The principal river of Messenia.
1599,570552,Panachaikon (mountain),The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Panachaikos Panachaikos.
1600,570555,"Panormos (settlement, port)","In the Barrington Atlas , John McK. Camp II located Pausanias' Panormos at a modern location he called ""Tekes"". Though Elliott has not been able to identify a settlement or locale in the area with such a name using online resources, the general area of Agios Vasilios/Prasino Limanaki is consistent with Pausanias' description and the location marked by Camp on BAtlas Map 58. An ancient settlement presumed to have been co-located with a harbor (limen) mentioned by Pausanias as lying 15 stadia east of the Rhion Pr. (modern Rio in Greece), on the north coast of the Peloponnese."
1601,570556,Panormos (harbor),"The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: harbor at Tekes An ancient harbor (limen) on the north coast of the Peloponnese, mentioned by Pausanias as lying 15 stadia to the east of the Rhion Pr. (modern Rio in Greece)."
1602,570564,Parrasia,A region of ancient Arcadia. A settlement of the same name is included in the Homeric catalog of ships.
1603,570565,Parthenias (river),"The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Bakireiko An ancient place, cited: BAtlas 58 B2 Parthenias fl."
1604,570567,Patra(e),"The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Patras Patra(e) (modern Patras) is an important ancient center with settlement beginning in the Late Helladic period. Patras played a leading role in the foundation of the second ""Achaean League"" and was the site of a Roman colony after 146 BC."
1605,570569,Pedion,"An ancient place, cited: BAtlas 58 B2 Pedion"
1606,570575,Pellana,The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Kalyvia Georgitsi An ancient settlement whose remnants are located at the modern village now bearing the ancient name (formerly Kalyvia Georgitsi) in Greece's Sparti municipality.
1607,570576,Pellene,The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Zugra Pellene was an ancient settlement in Achaea allied with Sparta during the Peloponnesian War.
1608,570577,Peloponnesus/Peloponnesos/Peloponnese,"The large peninsula protuding into the Mediterranean Sea that constitutes the southern part of Greece. It is largely separated from mainland Greece on the north by the Corinthian Gulf, joining it only in the northeast via the narrow Isthmus of Corinth."
1609,570579,Peneios (river),"The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Peneios An ancient place, cited: BAtlas 58 A2 Peneios fl."
1610,570588,Phalanthon M.,"The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: W Alonistaina An ancient place, cited: BAtlas 58 C2 Phalanthon M."
1611,570591,Pharis,The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Vapheio/Ag. Vasilios? Pharis or Phare was an ancient site in Laconia located in the Spartan plain along the route leading from Amyclae to the coast. It was abandoned by Pausanias' day. Shipley ventures a tentative identification with the area of modern Vapheio where there is evidence for a Bronze Age settlement with tholos tomb.
1612,570593,Pheia (island),"The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Tigani An ancient place, cited: BAtlas 58 A2 Pheia Ins."
1613,570595,Pheneos,"The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Kalyvia An ancient place, cited: BAtlas 58 C2 Pheneos"
1614,570598,Phigaleia,The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Phigaleia Phigaleia was an ancient city in the southwestern part of Arcadia in Greece.
1615,570601,Philanorion,"The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: N Bothiki An ancient place, cited: BAtlas 58 E2 Philanorion"
1616,570602,Phleious,The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Nemea An ancient city located in the valley of the river Asopos.
1617,570615,Pityoussa (island),"The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Spetsai A large island at the entrance to the Argolic Gulf, lying to the southwest off the tip of the peninsula of the Argolid. Modern Spetses."
1618,570616,Platamodes Pr.,"The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: near Marathopolis An ancient place, cited: BAtlas 58 B3 Platamodes Pr."
1619,570617,Plataniston (river),"The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Aspro Lankadi An ancient place, cited: BAtlas 58 B3 Plataniston fl."
1620,570625,Polichne,"The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Kopanaki/Stylari? An ancient place, cited: BAtlas 58 B3 Polichne"
1621,570634,Prote (island),"The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Proti An island in the Ionian Sea, located to the west of the Peloponnese that Thucydides mentions."
1622,570635,(Ps)Amathous,"The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: harbor at Porto Kagio An ancient place, cited: BAtlas 58 C5 (Ps)Amathous"
1623,570638,Psophis,"The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Psophis/Tripotamoi An ancient place, cited: BAtlas 58 B2 Psophis"
1624,570639,Pylos,"Pylos in Elis is mentioned in Xenophon, Diodorus, Strabo, and Pausanias (see Coleman 1986, Appendix 1 for ancient testimonia). The site was excavated by the American School of Classical Studies at Athens in 1968 and 1970 under emergency conditions ahead of the anticipated flooding of the site due to dam construction. The excavation report (Coleman) was finally published in 1986. An archaic through Roman settlement located at the Armatova hill, west of Agrapidochori in Ileia in the Peloponnese."
1625,570640,Pylos/Koryphasion,"The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: S Petrochorion A Classical settlement, probably the Pylos of Thucydides, on the Koryphasion promontory, (modern Akr. Koryphasiou in Messenia) in the Peloponnese."
1626,570653,Samikon/Samia,The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Kato Samikon A town of Triphylia in ancient Elis.
1627,570654,Saronicus Sinus,The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Saronic Gulf The Saronic Gulf (also called the Gulf of Aegina) is a part of the Aegean Sea that delimits the eastern side of the isthmus of Corinth.
1628,570657,Selemnos? (river),"The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Kastritsiou An ancient place, cited: BAtlas 58 B1 Selemnos? fl."
1629,570659,Selino(u)s (river near Krestena),"The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Selinous One of two rivers in the Peloponnese that bore this name, this Selino(us) was a late, left tributary of the Alpheious that flows past modern Krestena (the ancient city of Selino(u)s) and Makrisia (ancient Skillous) in the modern Elis Regional District. It is known today as the Selinountas or Selinous potamos."
1630,570661,Selinous (river),"The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Selinous An ancient place, cited: BAtlas 58 C1 Selinous fl."
1631,570662,Sellasia,"The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Palaiogoulas An ancient fortified settlement located a few kilometers north of ancient Sparta on a hill known in modern times as Palaiogoulas, which is east of the modern town of Sellasia. Sacked several times in antiquity, Pausanias reports the settlement was abandoned by his time."
1632,570664,Selleis? (river),"The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Seliandras An ancient place, cited: BAtlas 58 D1 Selleis? fl."
1633,570669,Side,"The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Velanidia? Pausanias tells us that the ancient settlement of Side was named for a daughter of Danaus and implies its location to have been somewhere on the Malea peninsula of mainland Greece, perhaps in the vicinity of Boiai (modern Neapoli Vion). Camp (BAtlas 58) tentatively places it at modern Velanidia."
1634,570673,Skandeia,"The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Ag. Nikolaos Pausanias locates Skandeia on the coast of the island of Cythera, some 10 stades from the inland settlement of Cythera."
1635,570674,Skillous,"The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Makrisia An ancient settlement, mentioned by Strabo, that was probably active from the Classical period through the early Roman empire. It was located in the vicinity of the modern Greek village of Makrisia (Elis regional unit of the Peloponnese)."
1636,570676,Skollis (mountain),"The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Skollis A mountain that Strabo reports as lying on the border of Elis and Achaea in the Peloponnese, identified with the modern Santameri/Santomeri/Santameriotiko (also now often called by its ancient name)."
1637,570679,Skyllaion (promontory),"The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Cape Spathi An ancient place, cited: BAtlas 58 F3 Skyllaion Pr."
1638,570700,Sythas (river),The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Trikalithos/Trikalitikos An ancient river of the northern Peloponnese (modern Trikaliotikos) that was considered to constitute the eastern border of the region of Achaia.
1639,570703,Tainaron (promontory),The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Akr. Tainaron Tainaron (Cape Matapan) is the southernmost point of mainland Greece.
1640,570704,Tan(a)os (river),"The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Tanos An ancient place, cited: BAtlas 58 D3 Tan(a)os fl."
1641,570707,Tegea,The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Piali/Episkopi Tegea was an ancient city of Arcadia. It is especially noted for its sanctuary dedicated to Athena Alea.
1642,570710,Temenion,"The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: near Nea Kios Temenion was located in the Argolid. It was built by Temenus, the son of Aristomachus. Temenion lay 50 stades from Nauplia and 26 from Argos."
1643,570711,Tenea,"The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: S Chiliomodi Tenea was an ancient city of the Corinthia famous for its sanctuary of Apollo. Scholars have long believed it is to be located in the area of modern Chiliomodi in Greece. Recent scientific excavations have identified the general extent of a large, multi-period cemetery zone to the east and south of the modern town, as well as an extensive bath complex of Roman date."
1644,570714,Teuthrone,"The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Kotronas An unexcavated ancient port settlement on the Gulf of Lakonia, located near modern Kotronas. There is some evidence of Bronze Age habitation on the Skopa peninsula and reports of a significant Classical-to-Roman complex on the mainland in the vicinity."
1645,570718,Theganoussa (island),"The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Venetiko Theganoussa island, the modern Venetiko, Peloponnese, Greece."
1646,570720,Theisoa,"The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Karkalous An ancient settlement of Arcadia. The archaeological site of the ancient acropolis is located at and around the thirteenth century Frankish castle, just south of modern Theisoa."
1647,570721,Th(e)isoa,"The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Thisoa/Lavda? An ancient place, cited: BAtlas 58 C2 Th(e)isoa"
1648,570723,Therapne,The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: SE Sparta Ancient settlement southeast of Sparta associated with the Menelaion (sanctuary of Helen and Menelaos).
1649,570733,Thouria,"The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Aithaia/Hellenika Thouria is a settlement of the Peloponnese, with archaeological evidence ranging in date from the Bronze Age to the Roman period. The nature of the archaic and classical polity is debated in the sources. The ancient site is located in the vicinity of modern Aithaia/Hellenika, about 3 kilometers north of modern Thouria."
1650,570735,Thyraion,"The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Palamari? An ancient town of Arcadia that was said to have been founded by Thyraeus, a son of Lycaon. It is possibly to be localized in the area of the modern village of Palamari in Greece's Trikolonoi municipality (Arcadia)."
1651,570737,Thyrides,The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Pounta A promontory on the west side of the central southern peninsula of the Peloponnese in Greece.
1652,570738,Tiasa (river),"The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Langada An ancient right tributary of the Eurotas, joining it south of ancient Sparta. It is to be identified probably with the modern Langada/Langkada (BAtlas) or Skatias (ToposText)."
1653,570741,Titane,"The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Titane An ancient settlement, long known to have been located near the modern town of Titani in Greece. It has been the subject of intensive archaeological excavation and survey only in the 21st century. The acropolis, of which significant fortification walls remain visible, is now occupied in part by the Church of Ag. Tryphon."
1654,570743,Touthoa (river),"The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: near Tsipoli An ancient river of the northwest Peloponnese, described by Pausanias as flowing into the Ladon at the border of Thelpusian and Heraian territory (i.e., prior to the Ladon's confluence with the Alpheios)."
1655,570749,Trikaranon (mountain),The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Koutsi Koutsi.
1656,570752,Trikrana (island),"The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Trikeri An ancient island mentioned by Pausanias, it can be identified with the modern Trikeri."
1657,570753,Trinasos,"The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Trinasos An ancient place, cited: BAtlas 58 D4 Trinasos"
1658,570754,Triphylia,"The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: S Elis, between R. Alpheios and R. Neda Triphylia was a region of the western Peloponnese located north of the Alpheius river and south of the Neda river."
1659,570756,Troizen,"The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Damala An ancient settlement, located in the Peloponnese."
