1674,573079,Althepia,"The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: near Troizen An ancient place, cited: BAtlas 58 unlocated Althepia"
1675,573086,Amymone,The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Argolis: spring at or near Lerna A river and homonymous spring mentioned by Pausanias in the vicinity of Lerna. Its precise location cannot be determined today.
1676,573089,Andania,"The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Arcadia: small town An ancient settlement, attested by literary or documentary sources, whose precise location cannot be determined today"
1677,573093,Anigros/Minyeios (river),"The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Triphylia: river near Samikon. Pausanias ( 5.5.11 ) relates that a cave sacred to the Anigrides, the river nymphs ( potamides ) of the river Anigros, was located near Samikon and was visited by those seeking relief from diseases of the skin. Pausanias describes this river near Samicum (Triyphylia) in Elis. He states that the river's currents frequently are held back by violent gales and that around the river mouth one finds quicksand. The river's precise location cannot be determined today."
