1801,579859,Amarynthos,"The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Palaiokhoria/Kato Vathia An ancient coastal settlement on the island of Euboea, located at modern Palaiokhoria/Kato Vathia (just east of the modern Amarynthos)."
1802,579860,Amphiale (promontory),The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: W Korydallos A promontory of Attica that is the terminus of the Aigaleos mountain range.
1803,579864,Anakaia?,The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Mygdaleza [VIII - inland? - 3] Anakaia (or Anacaea) was a deme of ancient Attica and a part of the phyle of Hippothontis. It is thought to have been located near modern Mygdaleza.
1804,579866,Anaphlystos,"The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Ag. Georgios [X - coast - 10(11)] A coastal deme of the tribe Antiochis in Attika, located on Anavyssos Bay."
1805,579867,Angele,"The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Angelisi [III - coast - 3/2(4)] An ancient place, cited: BAtlas 59 C3 Angele"
1806,579873,Aphidna,"The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: deme and fort, Kotroni [IX - inland - 16] A large Attic deme, located on the Gulf of Kotroni."
1807,579874,Aphrodite sanctuary at Dafni,"The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Daphni An ancient sanctuary of the goddess Aphrodite, described by Pausanias and located at modern Dafni (Daphne) along the ancient sacred way from Athens to Eleusis."
1808,579876,Araphen,"The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: W Raphina [II - coast - 2] An ancient place, cited: BAtlas 59 D2 Araphen"
1809,579879,Brauron/sanctuary of Artemis Brauronia,"The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Brauron Brauron was a sacred site in Attica dedicated to Artemis Brauronia. The sanctuary was active from the Middle Bronze Age period, although a gap in activity stretches from the Final Bronze Age to the eighth century B.C."
1810,579883,Atene,"The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: deme and fort, Charaka [X(XII) - coast - 3] Atene was a paralia (coastal) deme of Attica and belonged to the phyle Antiochis."
