1812,579886,Temple of Athena Skiras on Salamis,"The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Arapis This sanctuary, reported by Herodotus, is thought to have been located on the modern Cape Arapis in the northeast part of the island of Salamis, just north of the modern naval base. It is not to be confused with the Temple of Athena Skiras in Phaleron, reported by Pausanias."
1813,579887,Athmonon,"The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Amarousion [VII - inland - 6?(10?)] Athmonon was an ancient inland deme of the tribe Kekropis in Attica, north-east of the city of Athens at modern Marousi, best known as location of a sanctuary and festival of Artemis Amarysia."
1814,579888,Attica,"The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Attiki Historical region of Greece, centered on the Attic peninsula."
1815,579896,Boudoron,The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: SE Parama A settlement on the island of Salamis that was sieged by Cnemus in 429 BC.
1816,579902,Cholargos,"The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: near Kato Liosia [V - city - 4(6)] Cholargos was an ancient city deme of the tribe Akamantis in Attica, whose exact location is debated"
