1825,579925,Eretria (Euboea),The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Eretria Eretria was an ancient polis located in Euboea.
1826,579932,Euonymon,"The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Trachones [I- city 10 - (12)] A classical deme of Attica, located at modern Trachones / Ano Kalamaki. The area has been continuously exploited or inhabited by humans since at least the Neolithic period."
1827,579933,Eupyridai,"The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: near Kamatero [IV - inland - 2] An ancient place, cited: BAtlas 59 B2 Eupyridai"
1828,579935,Gargettos,"The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Ieraka [II(XI) - inland - 4(8?)] Gargettos was an inland deme of the tribe Aigeis in Attica, probably located south of Mt Pentalikon in the area of modern Gerakas."
1829,579939,Halai Aixonides,"The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Palaichori near Voula [VII - coast - 6(10)] Halai Aixonides was an Attic paralia deme of the Kekropis phyle. It was located near Cape Zoster on the western coast of Attica, south of the deme Aixones, from which the second part of its name derives."
1830,579940,Halai Araphenides,"The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Loutsa [II - coast - 5] A coastal deme of the tribe Aigeis, in Attica, located on the eastern shore north of Brauron. The site was known in antiquity for its sanctuary dedicated to Artemis Tauropolos."
1831,579941,Halimous,"The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: N Ag. Kosmas [IV - city - 3] Halimous was a city deme of the tribe Leontis, south of Athens at Cape Kolias, perhaps on the modern Hagia Anna hill."
1832,579942,Halipedon,The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: E Peiraieus A swampy plain that was located to the north of the main harbour of the Piraeus.
1833,579944,Hekale?,"The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Koukounarti [IV - inland - 1] Hekale was a deme of ancient Attica, likely situated in the plain of Marathon. It derived its name from Hecale, an old woman who aided Theseus in his hunt for the Marathonian bull and whom the hero subsequently honored."
1834,579946,Heleon,"The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Dritsa An ancient place, cited: BAtlas 59 A1 Heleon"
1835,579949,Hermos,The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Chaidari? [V - city - 2] Hermos was an Attic deme assigned to the tribe Acamantis.
1836,579955,Hymettos (mountain),"The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Ymittos Hymettos is a long mountain in Attica, which separates the plain (pedion) around the city of Athens from the interior of Attica (Mesogaia). It is divided into a northern section (Megas Hymettos) and a southern section (Anydros Hymettos) by the Pinari gorge. It was the site of marble quarries, forests, bee cultivation, and various cults."
1837,579958,Ikarion,"The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Dionyso [I(XI) - city* - 4/5(6)] An ancient settlement and inland deme of the tribe Aigeis, in Attica, said to be the birthplace of Thespis, the inventor of Greek drama."
1838,579959,Ilissos (river),"The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Ilissos Ilissos fl. is a river of Athens, Greece, that was originally a tributary of the Kifissos River. The Ilissos is now, for the most part, channeled below ground."
