1890,580097,Rhamnous,"The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: deme and fort, Rhamnous [IX - city* - 8] Rhamnous was an ancient settlement of Attica adjacent to the Euboean Strait and a coastal deme of the tribe Aiantis."
1891,580098,Rheitoi (river),The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Reitoi Pausanias describes this complex of two drainages near the Bay of Eleusis as sacred to Demeter and Persephone and as demarcating a territorial boundary between Athens and Eleusis. It was here that participants in the procession of the mystae were obliged to disembark from wagons and continue on foot to Eleusis. An inscribed decree of 422/421 BCE specifies the construction of a pedestrian bridge for this purpose.
1892,580104,Semachidai?,"The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Vredou [X - city* - 1] An ancient place, cited: BAtlas 59 C2 Semachidai?"
1893,580106,Soros,The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Marathonian Plain The tumulus (burial mound) of the Athenian dead at Marathon.
1894,580107,Sounion (Attica: settlement and deme),"The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: upper Agrileza valley [IV - coast - 4(6)] The fortified port settlement at Sounion, a coastal deme of Leontis, served the Athenian grain ships originating in Euboea and was the site of the sanctuary of Poseidon, among others."
1895,580108,Sounion (Attica: cape),"The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: promontory and fort, Kolonnes The southernmost tip of the Attic peninsula."
