1907,582862,Kydathenaion,"The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: N Acropolis [III(XI) - city - 11/12] Kydathenaion was the third largest deme of Attica, with only Acharnae and Aphidna being larger. It was located within the city walls of Athens and perhaps included the Acropolis and the Areopagus as well."
1908,582863,Melite,The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: W Agora [VII(XII) - city - 7] Melite was a deme of ancient Attica. It was located in the urban center of Athens and included both the Agora and the Pnyx. It belonged to the tribe of Kekropis.
