2320,741531,Nestou Epoikion,"The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Arsinoites/Krokodeilopolites Nomos An ancient village or region in the Arsinoite nome in Egypt, mentioned in documentary papyri, whose precise location cannot be determined today."
2321,741644,Trikomia,"The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Arsinoites/Krokodeilopolites Nomos An ancient place, cited: BAtlas 75 unlocated Trikomia"
2322,746710,Arabia Eudaemon,"The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: SAU Arabia Eudaemon or Arabia Felix was a term used by ancient geographers to describe the southern part of the Arabian Peninsula, now Yemen."
2323,746785,Nabataei,The Nabataei or Nabataeans was an ancient nation whose Arabian subjects lived in the Southern Levant and northern Arabia.
2324,756532,Aphroditopolis/Aphrodito,"The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Kom Isgaw Aphroditopolis was an ancient town of Egypt, modern Kom Isgaw."
2325,756566,Diospolis Mikra,"The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Hiw The capital of the seventh Nome of Upper Egypt, located on the west bank of the Nile."
2326,756574,Hermopolis Magna/Schmun,The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Ashmunein The capital city of the Hermopolite nome (the fifteenth Nome of Upper Egypt). The ancient Egyptians called the site Khmun after the group of eight divinities (Ogdoad) that represented the primordial world.
2327,756613,Panopolis/Schmin,The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Akhmim Capital city of the ninth (Chemmite) nome of Upper Egypt.
