2350,795846,Pselchis,"The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Dakka Eg.: Pselqet An ancient place, cited: BAtlas 81 C2 Pselchis"
2351,795866,Tachompso,"The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Djerar Eg.: Tekemsi An ancient place, cited: BAtlas 81 C2 Tachompso"
2352,805630,Meroe,"The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Bagrawiya Meroë is an ancient city located on the east bank of the Nile river near Shendi, Sudan. The city was a center of the kingdom of Kush."
2353,805634,Napata,The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Barkal Napata was a Nubian city-state located on the west bank of the Nile River and founded in the fifteenth century B.C.
2354,805639,Nubaei?,"An ancient place, cited: BAtlas 82 B4 Nubaei?"
2355,805647,Kawa,"The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Kawa Known today as Kawa, ruins of this ancient Egyptian and Kushite settlement are located on the east bank of the Nile river, seven kilometers south of the modern Nile bridge at Dongola in Sudan."
2356,814668,Chersonnesos Akra,"The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Ra's Abu Madd In describing features on the Red Sea coast of Arabia Felix, Ptolemy lists the Chesonnesos Akra. In the Barrington Atlas directory for Map 83, Graf suggests the Ras Abu Madd peninsula as a likely identification, but on the corresponding map, he labels a different feature: the mountainous Jabal Ral outcropping, about 120km north of Ras Abu Madd and some 40km east of the modern coastline."
2357,814688,Iathrippa,The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Medina Iathrippa was an oasis settlement along the Incense Road. From the Roman period until the advent of Islam the site was the seat of influential Iudaeo-Arabian tribes. Iathrippa would become an important center of Islam. Muhammad fled here from Mecca in 622 and the site was renamed Al-Madīna. It remained a key center until 656. It is the site of Muhammad's grave and a place of Muslim pilgrimage.
2358,814698,Aynuna,"The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: 'Aynuna SAU In modern Saudi Arabia, about 3km inland from the modern fishing port of al‑Khuraybah on the Gulf of Aqaba, a pair of ancient Nabatean sites occupy high ground to the northwest of the Wadi Aynuna. Settled since at least the Hellenistic period, Aynuna probably served as a Red Sea port for Petra. Most scholars agree that these sites are to be identified collectively with Leuke Kome, mentioned in Strabo and the Periplus of the Erythraean Sea; however, some other locations have been posited (see Gawlikowski 2022, note 5)."
2359,825217,Agaroi,"The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: NW Azov UKR An ancient place, cited: BAtlas 84 B2 Agaroi"
2360,825218,Agaron akron,"The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Berdyansk promontory UKR A promontory of the northern shore of the Azov Sea, included in Ptolemy's gazetteer. It is perhaps to be associated with the promontory that now extends into the sea near modern Berdyansk."
2361,825224,Aorsoi,The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: NE Caucasus RUS/UKR Aorsoi refers to a group of tribes of the Sarmatae living to the east of Maiotis.
2362,825237,Bata/Patous,The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Novorossiysk Bata/Patous was an ancient Greek colony on the Black Sea.
2363,825252,Dandarioi,"The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: E Azov An ancient place, cited: BAtlas 84 C3 Dandarioi"
2364,825255,Doschoi,"The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: E Azov An ancient place, cited: BAtlas 84 D3 Doschoi"
2365,825265,Gorgippia/Sindikos Limen,The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Anapa Gorgippia/Sindikos Limen was a sixth century B.C. colony founded by Pontic Greeks on the site of Sinda.
2366,825275,Iazamatai/Ixibatai,"The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: S Tanais An ancient place, cited: BAtlas 84 E1 Iazamatai/Ixibatai"
2367,825316,Lykos (river),The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Kal'mius UKR An ancient river placed by Ptolemy on the northern side of the Sea of Azov. It is probably to be identified with the modern Kal'mius river.
