2378,844847,Abonouteichos/Ionopolis,The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Inebolu A coastal town of Paphlagonia.
2379,844856,Amastris/Sesamos,"The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Amasra An ancient settlement on the Black Sea coast in Asia Minor, modern Amasra in Turkey."
2380,844857,Amnias (river),"The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: river An ancient place, cited: BAtlas 86 D2 Amnias fl."
2381,844879,Bithynion/Claudiopolis/Hadriana,"The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Bolu An ancient settlement in Bithynia, modern Bolu in Turkey."
2382,844915,Embolos,"The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Beyköy Robert argued for reading ""ἔμβολος"" in a fragmentary funerary epigram found in the area of Beyköy, Turkey, as a toponym. He argues, with reference to early travelers' accounts of antiquities in the area, for a nearby location for this putative settlement, probably up the gorge of the Ugursuyu."
2383,844926,Gangra,"The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Çankırı Also known as Germanicopolis or Germanopolis. An ancient settlement in Paphlagonia, modern Çankırı in Turkey."
2384,844949,Hypia/Hipius (mountain),"The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Kardüz Dağı A mountain mentioned in ancient sources, probably Kardüz Dağı in Turkey."
2385,844950,Hypios (river),"The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Büyük Melen Su / Akarsu. As Strobel ( New Pauly ) misidentifies the ancient Daphnutis lake as the Efteni Gölü, rather than the Ulubat Gölü, which is much further south and west, the Foss/Robert speculations about the identification of the upper course of the Hypios have been given certainty = ""less certain"" and the Strobel conjecture certainty = ""uncertain"". A river mentioned in ancient sources. Modern scholars identify it with the lower/larger (Büyük) course of the modern Melen Çay (Buyukmelen), which drains the marshy Efteni Golü (much diminished from its pre-modern extent). Ancient people seem to have extended the ""Hypios"" name past the lake and up one of its tributaries, but scholarly opinion is divided as to whether this was the modern Ugursuyu/Ogursu/Akarsu (Robert 1980, whence Foss in BAtlas) or the upper/smaller (Küçük) Melen Çayı (Strobel in New Pauly)."
2386,844970,Karambis (Pontus),The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Fakas? Karambis or Carambis was an ancient city of Paphlagonia. The ancient site is tentatively located near Fakas in Asiatic Turkey.
2387,844984,Kinolis,"The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Ginoğlu An ancient emporion on the southern coast of the Black Sea, mentioned in multiple ancient sources. It is probably to be identified with the subsequent site of ""Ginolu Kalesi"", a now-ruined 9th/10th century CE castle in the modern municipal territory of Çatalzeytin in Turkey's Kastamonu Province."
2388,844994,Kromna,"The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Tekeönü Kromna was a Milesian apoikía located on the Paphlagonian coast of the Black Sea, the modern Tekkeönü."
2389,845013,Mariandynoi,"The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: between Sangarius and Billaios fll. An ancient place, cited: BAtlas 86 A3 Mariandynoi"
2390,845026,Olgassys (mountain),The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Ilgaz Dağları Ilgaz Dağları.
