2413,854731,Satyrou Mnema,"The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: RUS An ancient place, cited: BAtlas 87 L2 Satyrou Mnema"
2414,854735,Sindike,The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: RUS Sindike was a region of the Taman peninsula inhabited by the ancient tribe of the Sindoi.
2415,854743,Theodosia,The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Feodosiya UKR A Greek colony founded by Miletus in the sixth century BC.
2416,854744,Tyrambe,The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Stanitsa Peresyp RUS A Greek settlement on the coast of the Sea of Azov.
2417,854745,Tyritake,"The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Arshintsevo UKR. Tolstikov (1997) describes the sequence of the site's fortification walls. A coastal settlement founded by Greeks, Tyritake is located about 11 km south of Kerch. The city's foundation dates to the middle of the sixth century BCE, although a Late Bronze Age settlement may have preceded the Greek colonial foundation. The city became a part of the Bosporan state and flourished until the late fourth century CE. It is noted for its circuit of fortification walls."
2418,857018,Amaseia,The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Amasya. The geographer Strabo was born in Amaseia ca. 64 BC. Amaseia (modern Amasya) was a naturally fortified settlement in the Pontic mountains near the Black Sea. It served as the capital of the kingdom of Pontus from ca. 300 BC to 183 BC.
2419,857022,Ameria (Pontos),"The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: near Ardıçlı, formerly Agustu An ancient settlement, associated with the sanctuary of Men Pharnakou in Pontos. It was located near modern near Ardıçlı (formerly Agustu) in Turkey's Tokat province."
