2425,857107,Dioscurias/Sebastopolis,The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Sukhumi GEO A Greek city established by Miletos ca. 540 B.C. on the site of an earlier second millennium B.C. settlement.
2426,857120,Euchaita,"The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Beyözü, formerly Avkat Euchaita was a Byzantine city and diocese located in Helenopontus, the Armeniac Theme of northern Asia Minor. The settlement was a station along the Roman road from Ancyra to Amasea."
2427,857133,Gazakene,"The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: district of Amaseia An ancient place, cited: BAtlas 87 A4 Gazakene"
2428,857134,Gazioura,"The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Turhal An ancient place, cited: BAtlas 87 B4 Gazioura"
2429,857148,Halys (river),"The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Kızıl Irmak The Kızılırmak river, the ancient Halys River, is a major river of Asia Minor that flows into the Black Sea."
