2441,857279,Phtheirophagoi?,"The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: GEO An ancient place, cited: BAtlas 87 F1 Phtheirophagoi?"
2442,857285,Polemonion/Side,"The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: between Fatsa and Boloman Irmak A harbor city on the Black Sea, Polemonion/Side was founded in the region of Sidene (Pontus) by either Polemon I or Polemon II of Pontus. Following the Roman annexation of the Pontic kingdom in the 60s CE, the city's importance declined substantially."
2443,857300,Sagylion,"The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Kaletepe An ancient place, cited: BAtlas 87 A3 Sagylion"
2444,857321,Sinope,"The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Sinop Sinope (modern Sinop, Turkey) on the Black Sea has been a major port since the time of the Hittites."
2445,857343,Taochoi,The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: in Oltu and Tortum Çay districts An ancient people that inhabited the South Caucasus and the mountainous region of northeastern Anatolia.
2446,857349,Theches (mountain),"The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Pontic Mts. in vicinity of Pontic passes A mountain and pass in the Pontic range near Trabazon where Xenophon says the 10,000 first sighted the sea. Its precise location cannot be determined today."
2447,857351,Thermai Phazemoniton,"The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Havza An ancient place, cited: BAtlas 87 A4 Thermai Phazemoniton"
