2450,857359,Trapezus,The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Trabzon An ancient settlement of Asia Minor on the south coast of the Black Sea. Modern Trabzon in Turkey.
2451,857382,Zela,"The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Zile Zela (modern Zile, Turkey) was an important ancient city of north-central Asia Minor; Strabo claimed Semiramis had founded the site. Iulius Caesar prevailed in the Battle of Zela against Pharnaces II of The Kingdom of Pontus, coining the phrase ""veni, vidi, vici""."
2452,857690,Auchis,"The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Taman’? An unlocated ancient city mentioned by Ptolemy and placed by him on the Psathis river, which is also unlocated. BAtlDir tentatively suggests Auchis may have been located in the area of modern Taman’ i.e. at the west end of the ancient Hermonassa island in the Kerch Strait."
2453,857726,Psathis (river),"The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: river, Taman’? An ancient river mentioned by Ptolemy whose location cannot be determined with certainty today. BAtlDir tentatively suggests it may have been located in the area of modern Taman’ i.e. at the west end of the ancient Hermonassa island in the Kerch Strait."
2454,860786,Ampsalis,"The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: near R. Mzymta? An ancient, unlocated city of Sarmatia mentioned by Ptolemy"
2455,860787,Asiba,"The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Pontus Polemoniacus inland An ancient place in Cappadocian Pontos, cited: BAtlas 87 unlocated Asiba"
