2517,903021,Ecbatana/Hagmatana/Achmeta/Epiphaneia/Ahmadan,"The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Hamadan. Hegmataneh was inscribed as a UNESCO World Heritage site in July 2024. The capital of Astyages (Istuvegü), captured by Cyrus the Great in 549 BCE. The site served as a summer residence for both Persian and Parthian kings."
2518,903045,Iasonius (mountain),"The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Kuh-i Damavand A mountain mentioned by Strabo, Ptolemy, and Ammianus. It is probably to be identified with Mount Damāvand in modern Iran."
2519,912806,Apamea,"The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: perhaps Famiya near Kut al-Amara; there appear to be two other places with the same name IRQ A city located on the Tigris, where it split into two streams, in the region of Mesene, founded by Antiochos I."
2520,912810,Arakia (island),"The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Kharg An island in the Persian Gulf, probably to be identified with the island of Kharg."
2521,912816,Babylonia,"The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: IRQ. In Rome's World: The Peutinger Map Reconsidered (2010), Richard Talbert notes that Konrad Miller seems to have overlooked this region name (viz. ItMiller 837-8). An ancient region in Mesopotamia."
